licant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SONY CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOKOYAMA TAKU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INOUE, MAKOTO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SONY CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOKOYAMA, TAKU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>INOUE MAKOTO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOKOYAMA TAKU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INOUE, MAKOTO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOKOYAMA, TAKU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A robot device capable of natural, autonomous motion, which has motion-induced emotional instinct models and is provided with a control means (32) for determining its motion by changing an emotional instinct model based on elements of input information (S1 to S3), whereby an autonomous action based on an emotional instinct condition of the robot device (1) itself can be permitted to implement a robot device capable of making natural motion autonomously.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un robot, capable de se déplacer de manière autonome, naturelle, et dont les modèles de comportement instinctif et émotionnel sont induits par ses déplacements ; en outre, ce robot est doté de moyens de commande (32) destinés à déterminer son déplacement par changement d'un modèle ce comportement instinctif et émotionnel, en fonction d'éléments d'informations d'entrée (S1 à S3). Ce robot (1) est caractérisé en ce qu'une action autonome, basée sur un état comportemental instinctif et émotionnel du robot, permet la mise au point d'un robot pouvant se déplacer de manière naturelle et autonome.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>